1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,200
So, apabila berlakunya kecemasan,

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:07,300
contohnya kita tengok, ada seorang lelaki rebah di klinik.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:11,100
Pesakit tidak ada respon dan tidak bernafas.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,100
Anda sebagai seorang petugas kesihatan,

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,300
apa yang perlu anda lakukan?

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,700
Assalamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuh.

7
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,000
Selamat pagi.

8
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,000
Hari ini kita nak berkongsi sedikit

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:30,800
pasal basic support untuk petugas kesihatan.

10
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,700
Sebelum tu, saya Muhammad Syahmi bin Mohd Sani,

11
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,800
pelajar program Bachelor of Medical Health Science,

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,600
kursus NBMH4143, teaching untuk healthcare professional.

13
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:52,300
Saya punya tutor adalah Sir Sivabalan anak lelaki Rajagopal.

14
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,400
So, apabila berlakunya kecemasan,

15
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,500
contohnya kita tengok, ada seorang lelaki rebah di klinik.

16
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,300
Pesakit tidak ada respon dan tidak bernafas.

17
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:07,300
Anda sebagai seorang petugas kesihatan,

18
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,500
apa yang perlu anda lakukan?

19
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:23,300
(peserta menjawab)

20
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:28,800
So, sebelum kita mula, objektif pembelajaran kita

21
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:33,900
ialah untuk terangkan urutan adult basic life support menggunakan DRSABCD.

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,600
Yang kedua, ia termasuk untuk menilai bahaya,

23
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:41,300
memeriksa respon dan minta bantuan serta memulakan CPR jika perlu.

24
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:47,700
Yang kedua, ialah menyatakan komponen utama dalam high quality CPR untuk orang dewasa.

25
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:54,600
First, kita tumpukan pada kedalaman tekanan, kadar tekanan

26
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,100
dan pengembangan dada penuh

27
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,500
atau full chest recoil untuk peredaran yang optimum.

28
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:05,600
Yang kedua, kita terangkan penggunaan AED yang selamat semasa cardiac arrest.

29
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:10,900
Kita kena faham langkah-langkah menghidupkan, memasang pad dan mengikuti arahan pada suara peranti.

30
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,700
Okay, faham?

31
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,300
Okay, sebelum kita mula tu,

32
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:20,900
kita nak terangkan pengenalan BLS dan chain of survival.

33
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,400
Dia ada 4 chain of survival dalam BLS. Yang pertama,

34
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,800
early access. Early access tu macam mana?

35
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,100
Early access tu sampai dapat kenal pasti.

36
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:40,000
Bila kita dapat kenal pasti, kita buat early CPR.

37
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:46,200
Okay, lepas tu bila dah early CPR, early defib.

38
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:52,600
Lepas tu, early ALS atau post-resuscitation care.

39
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:58,100
So, empat-empat komponen ni penting dalam BLS untuk memastikan kita dapat kualiti CPR.

40
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:06,000
Cardiac arrest, ataupun sudden cardiac arrest, apa maksudnya?

41
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,600
Jantung tu berhenti secara tiba-tiba dan tidak dijangka,

42
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:17,100
macam kita tengah makan atau apa-apa aktiviti.

43
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,300
Jantung tu tak bergerak.

44
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,300
Yang kedua,

45
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,200
aliran darah ke otak. Dia penting jantung ni

46
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:31,100
supaya aliran darah ke otak tu tidak terhenti lah.

47
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:36,900
Tanda-tanda dia: tidak responsif, pernafasannya tidak normal,

48
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,700
tiada nadi ataupun tiada aktiviti kehidupan.

49
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:44,700
Kalau apa pun yang berlaku dalam kategori ni,

50
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:48,100
kita kena ambil tindakan segera. Tindakan apa?

51
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:54,500
Danger first. First kita kena pastikan danger.

52
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:58,500
Danger kita kena pastikan ada tiga benda. Yang first,

53
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:04,500
kita sendiri, patient, dengan persekitaran.

54
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:08,800
Kalau untuk kita, at least kita kena pakai PPE:

55
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:11,800
glove, …, mask.

56
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:18,500
Untuk persekitaran, macam mana kalau kebakaran tu, kita kena keluar daripada kebakaran tu.

57
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:25,900
Yang kedua, check response. Macam mana kita nak check response kat patient?

58
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:32,400
Kita tap shoulder ni, kita tepuk bahu: "Okay, are you okay?"

59
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:34,500
Kalau dia tak ada bagi response,

60
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:41,300
kita shout for help. Macam mana nak bagi shout for help?

61
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:50,200
Kalau untuk healthcare worker, contoh kat wad ke apa, kita call bell tu, code blue, kita tekan.

62
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:57,500
Kita tekan, lepas tu minta seorang untuk bawa emergency trolley.

63
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:02,200
So kalau kat luar, kita shout lah kan.

64
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:05,100
Kita suruh orang, kita kena assign khusus.

65
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:09,000
Contohnya, "… tolong call 999, bawa AED."

66
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:16,500
Yang ketiga, yang keempat, open airway.

67
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,800
Open airway macam mana?

68
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:24,800
Untuk open airway, kita buat head tilt-chin lift.

69
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:29,600
Kalau patient trauma, kita tak galakkan, kita buat jaw thrust.

70
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:34,800
Cara nak open airway: kita pegang dagu dia,

71
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:41,300
kita tolak sikit, open airway dia.

72
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:46,900
Kita tak galakkan pegang kawasan ni, takut tutup airway tu.

73
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:55,900
A, B, C, D ni kita jalankan serentak. Kita open airway,

74
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:00,700
lepas tu kita tengok ada chest rise. Kita look, feel and listen.

75
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,600
Kita rasa dia punya hembusan ke tak.

76
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:07,500
Kalau tak ada chest rise, tak ada breathing,

77
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:12,700
sambil kita buka airway tu, kita rasa juga dia punya carotid pulse.

78
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:17,700
Kita check pulse untuk adult, kita check kawasan carotid.

79
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:21,400
So bila tak ada pulse, tak ada breathing, so kita terus…

80
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:29,400
So kena ingat, check pernafasan, check pulse, semua ni less than 10 seconds, semua jalan sekali.

81
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:35,900
Kita check pulse tadi, kalau tak ada, teruskan compression.

82
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:44,000
D, defib. Kalau ada defib, AED dah sampai, kita pasang AED lah.

83
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:56,400
Danger: PPE yang sesuai. Perhatikan darah atau objek tajam ataupun wayar elektrik.

84
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:59,800
Response: tap shoulder, okay?

85
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:05,000
Shout for help: aktifkan bantuan kecemasan dan minta AED, troli resusitasi.

86
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:11,800
Okay, untuk airway, kita buka, head tilt-chin lift tadi lah.

87
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:16,900
Lepas tu breathing: tengok, nilai 10 saat, tengok ada pernafasan normal ke tak.

88
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:23,800
Circulation: petugas kesihatan perlu menilai nadi mengikut latihan atau protokol.

89
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:27,200
Sekiranya tiada, terus buat compression.

90
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:36,200
Bila kita lakukan compression, dia ada 5 elemen high quality CPR.

91
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:51,100
30 compression.

92
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:57,200
Yang pertama, dia punya rate pada sekarang 100 ke 120 per minute.

93
00:07:57,300 --> 00:08:00,100
Kedalamannya 5 cm.

94
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:04,500
Bagaimana kita nak tahu 5 cm tu? Kita ukur pakai pembaris?

95
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:12,600
Bila kita tekan tu, macam bawah tu ada sekeras, itu anggaran 5 cm.

96
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:17,400
Lepas tu last kali, minimal interruption.

97
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:22,500
Contohnya kalau nak pasang AED, AED tu dah buka dulu siap-siap.

98
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:27,200
Kita tak nak tengah compress, berhenti, baru nak buka AED.

99
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:32,800
So kita nak melakukan demonstrasi.

100
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:37,600
So kalau untuk dewasa, 30 : 2.

101
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:47,300
So, demo compression ni, kita letak tangan kita kat middle sternum.

102
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:59,700
Okay, so kita tekan, kita pakai heel of palm.

103
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:04,800
Kita tekan, kita lock kita punya siku…

104
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:23,100
Yang terakhir, D, defib.

105
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:27,300
Defib, apa maksudnya defib?

106
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:37,500
Defib adalah satu peralatan mudah alih yang berkuasa bateri untuk menganalisis rentak jantung.

107
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:45,000
Kalau AED, untuk cardiac arrest, kita dapat selamatkan dia 70% ke 80%.

108
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:49,100
Kalau kita melakukan CPR sahaja, 5–6% saja.

109
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:56,800
Bila contohnya AED dah sampai, contohnya ini cardiac monitor,

110
00:09:56,900 --> 00:10:01,400
tapi pada monitor ni, dia ada function khas dia, AED.

111
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:08,200
So kita tak perlu nak tahu rhythm. Kalau orang awam, dia tak boleh nak baca rhythm,

112
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:13,100
untuk melakukan defib, so dia akan automatik.

113
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:18,700
So bila kita dah on, orang yang tengah CPR tu, dia terus compress sahaja.

114
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:24,100
Lepas tu, bila kita dah on, kita attach dia punya pad.

115
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:29,800
Pad ni kita attach kawasan sini ke sini.

116
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:42,200
Ya, betul. Bila kita attach tu, lepas tu dia akan bagi arahan:

117
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,500
"Don't touch patient, analysing rhythm."

118
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:54,400
Pastikan tiada siapa yang menyentuh semasa analisis dan kejutan.

119
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:58,400
Kalau dia kata continue CPR, kita terus.

120
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:05,800
Kalau dia kata shock advised, kita akan tekan butang shock di sini.

121
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:15,300
Okay, ini tindakan selepas defib tu.

122
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:20,500
Kita dah pasang defib, dia ada shock advised dengan no shock advised.

123
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:24,400
Kalau shock advised tu, kena pastikan semua orang jauh.

124
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:29,500
Selepas, kita gunakan: "You clear, I clear, everybody clear."

125
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,300
Okay, tindakan selepas buat CPR tu,

126
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:39,000
selepas bagi shock tu, kita teruskan CPR selama 2 minit

127
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:42,500
dan sehingga AED minta balik.

128
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:45,800
Kita continue compress, lepas tu dah 2 minit tu,

129
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:50,500
AED tu akan automatik stop CPR, analysing rhythm.

130
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:54,700
Lepas tu kalau no shock advised, sambung CPR. Dia akan bagi arahan,

131
00:11:54,800 --> 00:12:01,200
dia sama ada bagi pada skrin tu ataupun bagi secara audio.

132
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:06,300
Soalan.

133
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:11,000
Apakah maksud D dalam DRSABCD?

134
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,100
(peserta) Danger. — Danger, betul.

135
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:17,700
Berapa kadar mampatan untuk dewasa?

136
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:20,200
(peserta) 100–120.

137
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:24,300
Apakah kedalaman mampatan tu?

138
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,400
(peserta) 5–6.

139
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:42,200
Selepas AED bagi arahan, apakah tindakan yang seterusnya?

140
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:44,900
(peserta) CPR.

141
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:53,700
Kalau AED tu bagi arahan shock advised…

142
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:59,400
Clear… everybody clear, tekan shock.

143
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:07,800
Rumusannya.

144
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:15,700
So untuk basic life support ni, ni dia punya mantra dia lah:

145
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:19,300
D-R-S-A-B-C-D.

146
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:24,600
D, defib. Kalau ada, kita dapat bantu dia dengan cepat lah.

147
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:28,400
Untuk last kali, high quality CPR.

148
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:31,600
Yang pertama, rate 100 ke 120.

149
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,600
Push hard,

150
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:39,400
lepas tu dia punya 30 : 2. Kedalaman 5–6 cm.

151
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,800
Full chest recoil. Full chest recoil ni macam mana?

152
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:49,100
Dia macam spring, kita tekan, naik balik.

153
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:53,800
Bukan macam ni, dia kena naik balik.

154
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:56,700
Last kali, minimal interruption.

155
00:13:56,800 --> 00:14:01,900
Dia akan ada interruption, contohnya tengah CPR tu,

156
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:07,900
ataupun sementara nak tukar, change CPR tu, itu interruption.

157
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,700
So kita kena minimumkan.

158
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:16,400
So yang paling penting, chain of survival: early access, early CPR,

159
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:21,600
early defib, early ALS ataupun post-resuscitation care.

160
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:25,900
So kalau dah ada pulse, dah ada breathing,

161
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:32,000
so cara nak buat recovery position.

162
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:40,900
Supaya kita dapat pantau dia lah.

163
00:14:57,600 --> 00:15:00,800
Kalau macam nak tunggu ICU ke, masuk ICU ke,

164
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,800
Ni antara rujukan saya:

165
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:15,000
MOH NCORT BLS Subcommittee 2021–2025,

166
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:21,900
National Committee on Resuscitation Training Guidelines,

167
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:27,300
ILCOR Consensus on CPR and ECC Science 2020,

168
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:32,600
European Resuscitation Council Guidelines for Resuscitation 2021,

169
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:39,100
American Heart Association Guidelines Update for CPR and ECC 2020.

170
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:42,800
Ini antara rujukan yang kita praktikkan.

171
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:50,100
Ada apa-apa soalan?

172
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,200
Terima kasih.
